    {
      "id": "brbg4gv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gdacjcb",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rvjha42",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "772qst2",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "ccrunyg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "npxvzmz",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x12dwpt",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tpgkz2o",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Litmus indicator turns RED in acids and BLUE in bases.",
        "Phenolphthalein remains COLORLESS in acidic medium and turns PINK in basic medium.",
        "Acid rain has a pH value lower than 5.6 due to dissolved oxides of nitrogen and sulfur.",
        "Plaster of Paris (CaSO4·1/2H2O) converts to Gypsum (CaSO4·2H2O) upon hydration."
      ],
      "id": "up66gtn"
    },
    {
      "id": "3oxy5ke",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1qswr6r",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2wh2wy7",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9mzmh5o",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "b8un09b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9e44aem",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "unsh0ds",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e3vi67z",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7h01ik8",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}